    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline woes",
          "heading": "Mesake Doge sent off as Fiji Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV",
          "body": "Fiji Latui's discipline unravelled at Virgin Media Park on Friday night: four first-half yellow cards, three of them inside five minutes, left the second-string side down to 12 men for a spell. Mesake Doge's first yellow was for a high tackle on Todd Lawlor; 30 seconds after returning he collected a 20-minute red for collapsing a third consecutive scrum. Pita Lesivoukionoilau's interception try had given the visitors their only lead in the seventh minute, and Jope Naseara added a breakaway score."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north. Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Haka tribute",
          "heading": "Lewis Moody faces the haka alongside England before 37-12 All Blacks rout",
          "body": "The former England captain, diagnosed with motor neurone disease last year, stood between Maro Itoje and Ellis Genge as England faced the challenge, then watched from the stands as they won 37-12 on Saturday. He had presented the shirts on Friday night, and Steve Borthwick told BBC Radio 5 Live that Moody \"spoke unbelievably in the way he put his message across and it really resonated with the players.\" Every England player wore boots carrying the logo of his Front Up to MND campaign."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north. Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Final booked",
          "heading": "France's 45-17 bonus-point win over Argentina books Twickenham final against Springboks",
          "body": "Seven tries, five after the break, earned France the attacking bonus point in Saturday's 45-17 win over Argentina at the Stade de France, edging them past England to top the Europe pool on 25 points. Fabien Galthié's side now face South Africa in the Nations Championship final at Twickenham, a rematch of their 21-19 win in Saint-Denis earlier this month. Rugbyrama's ratings flagged a worry: Aaron Grandidier-Nkanang went off just after the hour with an apparent muscle injury, though replacement Emilien Gailleton scored with his first ball."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north",
          "body": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Twickenham, London"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Kiss reunion",
          "heading": "Ireland will face former defence coach Les Kiss in fifth-place play-off",
          "body": "After Saturday's 20-17 win over South Africa, Andy Farrell's side finished third in the Northern Hemisphere ladder. The42 reports that this sets up a meeting with Australia at Twickenham in the Nations Championship finals weekend. Kiss, Ireland's ex-defence coach and a former Ulster boss, succeeded Joe Schmidt as Wallabies head coach earlier this year. His side sealed third in the Southern Hemisphere table by edging Wales 29-26 on Saturday. France and South Africa contest the final."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Twickenham, London"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "The42"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Simone Ferrari's late injury forces Italy front-row reshuffle before Fiji defeat",
          "body": "Italy lost 16-21 to Fiji in Udine on Saturday without Simone Ferrari, ruled out about an hour before kickoff with an injury to his left upper limb, OnRugby reported. Marco Riccioni was promoted from the bench to start at tighthead, with Ion Neculai taking the No. 18 shirt. Ferrari will be assessed in the coming days to gauge his recovery time, with the Fiji rematch ahead. Despite the reshuffle, captain Giacomo Nicotera said Italy's scrum had done good work and was becoming a weapon."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north. Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "OnRugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury worry",
          "heading": "Townsend hopes Matt Fagerson injury is not serious before Twickenham finals weekend",
          "body": "Saturday's 67-5 rout of Japan at Murrayfield came with one back-row worry for Gregor Townsend, who singled out his starting No. 8 afterwards: \"Matt Fagerson went through a lot of work and hopefully his injury isn't serious.\" The 11 tries left Scotland fourth in the northern hemisphere table but with a vastly improved points difference, and the head coach said his side still don't know what their week will look like before finals weekend at Twickenham."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north. Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Officiating row",
          "heading": "Dewi Lake's TMO plea ignored after Tupou's alleged strike on Alex Mann",
          "body": "Saturday's 26-29 defeat to Australia has left viewers fuming at the officials. After Wales won a scrum penalty, footage appeared to show Wallabies prop Taniela Tupou aim a swinging forearm at Alex Mann's midriff. Captain Dewi Lake told referee Luc Ramos that Australia's No. 3 had punched Wales' No. 6 and urged a TMO review, WalesOnline reports, but neither the referee nor the TMO acted. Tupou scored the opening try shortly afterwards and could yet be cited."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Red-card rout",
          "heading": "Pumas crushed 45-17 by France after Mayco Vivas red card in Paris",
          "body": "Argentina's 45-17 defeat at the Stade de France unravelled after the hour. Hollie Davidson's yellow for Mayco Vivas was upgraded to red, and Julián Montoya's later yellow left the Pumas 13 against 15. The damage had started early: Santiago Chocobares withdrew hours before kick-off, and Bautista Delguy and Boris Wenger went off without returning. Justo Piccardo's try from inside centre and Tomás Albornoz's boot put the visitors 10-7 up. Pablo Matera's interception was the only second-half reply. Scotland await in a battle for seventh."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north",
          "body": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Americas Rugby News"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Play-off set",
          "heading": "Wallabies' Cardiff win over Wales sets up Ireland fifth-place play-off",
          "body": "The 29-26 result sealed third in the Southern Hemisphere table of the Nations Championship, so Les Kiss' side meet Andy Farrell's Ireland, third in the Northern Hemisphere ladder, for fifth place at Twickenham, The42 reports. The win also ended a run of four defeats, per the Guardian. Len Ikitau's 64th-minute try and a late Carter Gordon penalty left Wales needing a try they never found. Their final attack broke down with a forward pass, SA Rugby Magazine reports."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
        }
      ],
