    "465": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rematch set",
          "heading": "All Blacks miss Nations Championship final and face England again for third",
          "body": "South Africa pipped New Zealand to top spot in the southern-hemisphere table, and France's win over Argentina took them past England, the Guardian reports. That sends the All Blacks straight back into a third-place final against the side that beat them 37-12 at Allianz Stadium on Saturday. It was the widest margin New Zealand have ever lost by to northern-hemisphere opposition. Maro Itoje already has the rematch in view: \"We don’t want this to be our ceiling, we don’t want this to be as good as we get.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 to reach Springboks final",
          "body": "Ireland beat South Africa 20-17 to finish third in north. Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to finish third in south. Fiji's second-string Latui lose 62-12 to Ireland XV."
